1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,560
So you really don't want to tell them you're leaving? Are you sure about that?

2
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:10,640
Yes. With the training those two are going through right now, every last moment counts.

3
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:12,980
Tell them we'll meet again.

4
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:14,260
Yeah.

5
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:15,680
So long.

6
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:17,920
Goodbye, Leorio.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,120
Hey, hold on a second.

8
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:23,180
Keep an eye on him for me, will ya?

9
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:26,540
He acts calm, but he can be reckless.

10
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:29,500
He's smart, but he doesn't always think things through.

11
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:35,240
I see he opens up to you more than most people. Do you think you can keep him in check?

12
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:39,880
Sure. You're very soothing, you know.

13
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:44,560
Of all the heartbeats in this city, yours is the most pleasant.

14
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:49,500
It's uplifting, incredibly gentle, and very warm, too.

15
00:00:50,220 --> 00:00:53,900
I think you'd make an excellent teacher, or maybe even a doctor.

16
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:58,100
I would recommend a career change.

17
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,420
I might have to give it some thought.

18
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:09,360
Time for me to get serious and hit the books.

19
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:10,660
I think it's alright.

20
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:11,520
Thanks.

21
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:17,180
I think it's katie.

22
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:23,620
I am low when I grow down,

23
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:26,480
I appear to stand my turn of Heaven,

24
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:31,420
I make you turn on my path.

25
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:41,740
You ain't one but alone

26
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:48,740
You can fly away.

27
00:01:48,740 --> 00:01:52,740
You can fly away.

28
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:57,740
You can fly away.

29
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:01,740
The world is your shining.

30
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:05,740
The sun is shining.

31
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:07,740
You will shine.

32
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:09,740
The moon is shining.

33
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:39,720
We'll see you next time.

34
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:54,820
Number 16 wins Green Island for $27.8 billion!

35
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:58,460
Thank you very much!

36
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:05,180
That bastard's out to get every single copy, and he knows exactly what my budget is!

37
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:12,480
There's only one copy left, and it's gonna be mine, damn it!

38
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:15,380
What? He left?

39
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:19,380
He'll be back. He said to keep training hard.

40
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:22,920
Aw, he didn't have to worry about that.

41
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:27,800
Wait a minute, I could have sworn that you were happy Kurapika was leaving York New City.

42
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:31,300
Well, sure I was happy. I just wanted to say bye.

43
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:37,340
Here. For you from Zepile. He said you'll see him again.

44
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:40,520
Huh? Mr. Zepile too?

45
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,720
Yeah, and he recovered your hundred million jenny, just like he said he would.

46
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:46,520
He really did.

47
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:49,600
Now you can buy your hunter's license back from the pawn shop.

48
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:54,160
Yeah. Mr. Zepile's awesome! I mean really awesome!

49
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:01,860
Man, that hunter's license sure is incredible.

50
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:06,580
The pawn shop forked over a hundred million on the spot.

51
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:10,200
Probably could have added a couple more zeros if it was sold at auction.

52
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:18,600
Hey, I know! I should become a professional hunter so I can sell my license!

53
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:22,740
And forget all about debt! I could live off the interest alone, easy!

54
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:25,960
All right, let's get cracking! There's no time to waste!

55
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:28,440
I gotta start prepping for the hunter exam!

56
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:34,300
Number 16 wins Greed Island for $60.2 billion!

57
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:38,180
Thank you very much!

58
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,400
$60.2 billion?

59
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:42,720
That's unheard of!

60
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:46,020
And to think he managed to win all seven copies up for auction!

61
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:49,680
I know, I know! But it cost him half his fortune!

62
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:57,680
An unknown party stole a copy of Greed Island won by Mr. Batera for $30.5 billion.

63
00:04:57,680 --> 00:05:05,540
Not to be discouraged, he won copies for $27.8 billion yesterday and won for $60.2 billion today.

64
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:09,880
Hmph! There must be some reason he went so far for a video game.

65
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:14,640
I hear if you beat it, that you receive an actual treasure map at the very end.

66
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:18,700
Or that a giant dragon appears and offers to grant you a wish.

67
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:21,780
There are all kinds of rumors out there.

68
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:23,980
Thank you!

69
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:28,660
I'm going home.

70
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:36,380
Earlier today, Mr. Batera won all the copies of Greed Island.

71
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:39,560
But he's also seeking players to play the game.

72
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,760
Today's the deadline.

73
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,680
There's already an amazing line outside the venue!

74
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:47,360
I apologize for the long wait, everyone.

75
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,900
We will now begin selecting the players.

76
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:55,360
And as you're already aware, you must be capable of using Nen in order to play.

77
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:58,440
The test will proceed as follows.

78
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,200
First, we will need each applicant to demonstrate their Nen.

79
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:06,620
Once the demonstration phase is complete, we will make our decision.

80
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:12,020
The judge will be none other than professional hunter, Mr. Tezgera!

81
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,540
The jackpot hunter Tezgera?

82
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:15,360
Wow!

83
00:06:15,780 --> 00:06:19,060
If he's involved, this game must pay huge dividends!

84
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:24,280
Alright, we will now begin the test.

85
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:28,380
Come up one at a time and show me your Ren.

86
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:34,540
A curtain will block any view of the stage, so the other applicants can't see what's happening.

87
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:39,880
The test will be over, as soon as we've chosen all 32 of our players.

88
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:46,480
To participate, step this way and form a line!

89
00:06:56,820 --> 00:06:58,360
That's all they're telling us?

90
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:02,860
Would the first applicant please step in?

91
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:06,480
That explanation was so vague, we don't know anything.

92
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:11,740
But the others are stepping up like it's the only natural response.

93
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:13,860
They must know.

94
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:17,240
It's pretty obvious those guys aren't gonna answer any questions.

95
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:20,580
Our task is simple.

96
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:23,860
Deduce all we can from the information provided.

97
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:25,720
Then try our best.

98
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,740
So they're judging us on the entire process.

99
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:31,160
They've gotta be.

100
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:34,500
There are about 200 people in the hall.

101
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,820
Around 100 have already lined up.

102
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:41,980
And at least 50 are still watching closely from the sidelines.

103
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:46,100
And 20 who haven't moved an inch.

104
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,980
Which group made the right choice?

105
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:51,320
Next up please.

106
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:53,960
Next!

107
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:57,480
Hold on.

108
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,940
Ten people have gone in.

109
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:02,360
But nobody has come back out again.

110
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:06,780
Does that mean everyone who went in passed?

111
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:08,260
This is bad.

112
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,700
Should we get in line?

113
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:13,200
Those guys are hopeless.

114
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:15,820
They don't stand a chance of getting in.

115
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:19,300
I'm talking about the ones still in line.

116
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:21,000
And those who are waiting nearby.

117
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,260
But the ones who are hovering next to the line are really hopeless.

118
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:30,740
They're probably waiting around for someone to return so they can ask them what's waiting inside.

119
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:34,080
If only they'd done a little bit of research.

120
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:35,760
Or just thought for a second.

121
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:39,340
Then maybe they'd see there's no point in rushing to the front.

122
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,220
In other words, it's impossible to send in new players.

123
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:49,820
That's why I'm so careful selecting players.

124
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:51,500
I get it now.

125
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:55,040
They're not choosing 32 players this time, are they?

126
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:56,700
No, they are not.

127
00:08:57,300 --> 00:09:00,920
It's been over 10 years and not a single player has cleared the game.

128
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:06,120
And as you know, new players can't start Greed Island as long as the old ones are still alive.

129
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:15,660
So of course, what that really means is they have to save a few spots just in case any extraordinary players pop up and want to join in on the action.

130
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:21,020
And if I had to hazard a guess, they'll only add about 20 or so in this round.

131
00:09:21,020 --> 00:09:28,260
Personally, I'd say that the ones in line or the ones standing nearby have no shot whatsoever.

132
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:37,360
Anybody worthwhile either stood up and got in line just as soon as possible, or figured out the trick and stayed in their seats to focus like we did.

133
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:39,280
Wouldn't you agree, kid?

134
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:45,100
Gon, you figured out what was going on?

135
00:09:45,980 --> 00:09:48,020
Well, yeah, but it was only a hunch.

136
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:50,020
I just thought it was only natural.

137
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:52,520
They want to test everybody who's here, don't they?

138
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:55,980
And if that's the case, what does it matter if we get in line or not?

139
00:09:57,820 --> 00:09:58,860
Very true.

140
00:09:59,060 --> 00:09:59,920
You win, kid.

141
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:00,920
Nice thinking.

142
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:03,260
Yeah, that's pretty impressive.

143
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:07,060
Not many people can commit to their own logic like you just did.

144
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:09,140
Nope, not many people at all.

145
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:16,280
The steeper and more dangerous the path, the better it is to turn half your brain off or you'll never be able to take the plunge.

146
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:18,500
All right then. Next, please.

147
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:22,660
The name's Puhat, by the way.

148
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,360
Well, nice to meet you.

149
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:29,140
The people who act like they're smart are the ones that usually fail.

150
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:31,320
You know we can hear you.

151
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:34,140
Still, he's telling the truth.

152
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:37,700
I was too focused on logically making the right move.

153
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:41,040
I'm going ahead.

154
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,540
Right. Good luck.

155
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:47,500
If I'm not willing to take chances, I'll never advance.

156
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:52,660
Listen, never take risks.

157
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:58,180
Only act when success is 100% guaranteed.

158
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:00,120
Otherwise, wait.

159
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:02,860
Waiting is our most crucial job.

160
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:10,460
If victory isn't assured, revealing your strength is the most foolish move you can make.

161
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:13,240
That's my old man's logic.

162
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:15,900
But I'm not an assassin.

163
00:11:16,460 --> 00:11:17,480
I'm a hunter.

164
00:11:18,620 --> 00:11:21,240
All right, kid. Now let me see your Ren.

165
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:22,820
Hatsu okay?

166
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:24,620
That'll be fine.

167
00:11:25,060 --> 00:11:28,220
You can show me anything that properly demonstrates your power.

168
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:32,460
Prove to me that you can do better than the Ren I saw earlier.

169
00:11:33,420 --> 00:11:34,180
All right then.

170
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:35,680
Here goes.

171
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:47,000
He changed his aura into electricity.

172
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:50,180
It's possible in theory, of course.

173
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:53,820
But the fact that he learned it from scratch in only four days is unbelievable.

174
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:58,000
Well, do you need to see any more?

175
00:11:58,400 --> 00:11:59,700
No, you've passed.

176
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:01,120
That's enough.

177
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:07,740
But this technique couldn't have fully developed over nights.

178
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:11,020
You would have to be exposed to enormous amounts of electricity.

179
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:12,520
It would take years.

180
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:14,200
Who are you?

181
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:16,660
Electricity's nothing.

182
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:19,220
Been shocked since I was born.

183
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,820
Family circumstances, you see.

184
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:40,980
Seven people.

185
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:43,000
That guy was right.

186
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:46,100
The people who passed were the ones who got up immediately,

187
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:48,360
or the ones who waited in their seats.

188
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:51,920
Well, I hope Gon's doing okay.

189
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:52,020
Okay.

190
00:12:52,020 --> 00:13:03,280
Goon!

191
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:04,500
Killua!

192
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:06,620
That's awesome!

193
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
You got chosen, huh?

194
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:08,980
Of course I did.

195
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,440
That big sound was you, wasn't it?

196
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:12,020
Yup!

197
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:15,120
Honestly.

198
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:19,020
Those two kids are really something else.

199
00:13:19,020 --> 00:13:23,600
Allow me to be the first to congratulate you.

200
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:28,340
The 21 people still here have earned the right to play Greed Island.

201
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:32,640
You will receive 50 billion jenny upon clearing the game.

202
00:13:33,380 --> 00:13:35,600
All the details are there in the contract,

203
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,380
so be sure to read it thoroughly,

204
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:40,500
and sign it before you leave here at 5 p.m.

205
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:42,720
Cheers!

206
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:46,480
Congrats on making it past stage one!

207
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,060
Could you look at this for us?

208
00:13:49,020 --> 00:13:49,500
What?

209
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:52,080
Contract, huh?

210
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:56,440
It can be summed up in three points.

211
00:13:57,120 --> 00:14:00,460
First, you can't file any claims if you're injured or you die.

212
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:04,940
Second, any items you bring out of the game belong to Mr. Batera.

213
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:09,920
Third, if you clear the game, you receive a 50 billion jenny reward.

214
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,620
I don't see any problems.

215
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:13,200
Good!

216
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,280
Just sign it and you're all set.

217
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:16,940
Point two seems important.

218
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:21,260
It talks about any item that you might bring out of the game.

219
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:25,100
He's offering an enormous reward, and that's why.

220
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:26,740
Yeah, but what kind of items?

221
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:28,060
I don't care.

222
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:30,520
Because I'm not playing for items.

223
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:33,980
I just want to get as close as possible to Gene.

224
00:14:40,940 --> 00:14:42,120
Well, see ya.

225
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:44,100
Good luck on your exam, Leorio.

226
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:45,020
Thanks.

227
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:46,820
You two be careful, okay?

228
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:49,060
You'll be a doctor next time we see you.

229
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:53,020
Wait, does that mean we won't see each other for at least four years?

230
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:55,120
We're going to clear that game fast.

231
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:56,800
It isn't going to take that long.

232
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:58,860
Then I'll be ready.

233
00:14:59,020 --> 00:14:59,240
Hmm.

234
00:14:59,240 --> 00:14:59,580
Good luck.

235
00:15:01,580 --> 00:15:03,380
Good luck.

236
00:15:03,380 --> 00:15:04,980
Good luck.

237
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:06,840
Good luck.

238
00:15:07,020 --> 00:15:07,780
Pretty-hmm.

239
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:08,880
Good luck.

240
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:10,100
Good luck.

241
00:15:10,460 --> 00:15:10,760
Good luck.

242
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:12,000
Good luck.

243
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:12,280
Good luck.

244
00:15:12,460 --> 00:15:12,800
Good luck.

245
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:13,500
Good luck.

246
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:14,020
Oof.

247
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:16,420
Good luck.

248
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:17,620
Good luck.

249
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:19,200
You guys are together.

250
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:20,580
You're surrounded by the group.

251
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:21,700
Come.

252
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:22,080
Good luck.

253
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,400
You're a little palm.

254
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:24,900
You're welcome.

255
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:26,200
Good luck.

256
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:27,340
Good luck.

257
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:28,060
Thank you.

258
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:46,320
Now then, I'll just explain a few things before we begin.

259
00:15:46,940 --> 00:15:50,440
The individual game copies are not independent of each other.

260
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:56,060
No matter which console you start from, you'll all arrive at the same place.

261
00:15:56,060 --> 00:16:01,040
Think of it as a virtual area, accessible from any spot on this planet.

262
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:05,520
I'll hand out memory cards to each of you.

263
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:08,260
Once I do, head straight into the game.

264
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:10,640
But first, we'll decide the order.

265
00:16:11,340 --> 00:16:11,780
Order?

266
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:16,080
The game only allows one player at a time to enter into it.

267
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:20,120
We'll decide now to avoid any bickering inside the game.

268
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,360
Fine. Then how about rock, paper, scissors?

269
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:27,440
Yes! I'm first!

270
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:33,180
Hold on. Aren't you the one who's already obtained a save file?

271
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:35,880
Oh, damn it. I'm number 17.

272
00:16:38,460 --> 00:16:40,200
Would you like to use it?

273
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:48,780
Don't worry. Your initial destination is always the same, regardless of your save file.

274
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:50,100
Gene.

275
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:53,960
This game is a message from him to me.

276
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:56,600
I'm gonna trust him.

277
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:01,200
I'm gonna go for it. I'll use my own card.

278
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:05,580
Okay. Then put the ring on, and whenever you're ready to go, begin.

279
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:06,380
Go.

280
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:09,340
Wait for me in the starting area, okay?

281
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:10,340
Hmph.

282
00:17:10,340 --> 00:17:28,300
The next person can go as soon as the screen says, now playing.

283
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:50,800
Welcome to Greed Island, sir. You must be go'n freaks.

284
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:54,820
I will explain how the game works. Would that interest you?

285
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:55,600
Sure.

286
00:17:56,660 --> 00:18:01,840
In this game, anyone who is wearing a ring has two spells available to them.

287
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:04,120
They are called Book and Gain.

288
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:08,680
Place the hand wearing the ring in front of you, and say Book.

289
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:10,740
Uh, Book!

290
00:18:10,740 --> 00:18:18,240
You see, your task is to seek out and collect certain cards.

291
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:21,460
That binder is for storing all of the cards you've collected.

292
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:24,380
Now please take a look at the first page.

293
00:18:25,300 --> 00:18:27,060
Each slot is labeled with a number.

294
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:32,140
With these, you can only place a card if its number corresponds with the one on the slot.

295
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:34,280
These are your specified slots.

296
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,200
Please flip ahead a few pages.

297
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:40,140
Wait, these aren't numbered.

298
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:41,360
That's right.

299
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:44,700
With these slots, you can place any card you choose.

300
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:46,820
These are called your free slots.

301
00:18:47,840 --> 00:18:51,840
Specified slots are numbered 0 to 99, making 100.

302
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:55,720
Then, you have another 45 free slots.

303
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:59,980
To clear the game, you must fill the 100 specified slots.

304
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:02,920
Then, and only then, will you be successful.

305
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:06,940
So I just need to collect 100 cards, huh?

306
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:07,720
Correct.

307
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:14,040
More specifically, you must obtain 100 items, and after transforming them, put them in your binder.

308
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:14,760
Transform?

309
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:16,080
That's correct.

310
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:20,820
If you obtain a sword, for example, it will instantly transform into a card.

311
00:19:21,540 --> 00:19:26,040
If you wish to use a card as the item, you must first use the spell Gain.

312
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,800
I get it.

313
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:35,160
However, once you've returned a card to item form, you can never transform it into a card again.

314
00:19:35,660 --> 00:19:39,660
If you want the card version of the item, you must once again acquire it.

315
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:41,220
Make sense so far?

316
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:43,860
Uh, I think so.

317
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:47,660
Now, there are two other cases where an item can't become a card.

318
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:53,020
In the first of those two cases, you reach the item's maximum conversion limit.

319
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:55,320
Wait, card conversion limit?

320
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:56,320
Yes.

321
00:19:56,840 --> 00:20:00,840
Every item in this game has a limit to the number of times it can be converted.

322
00:20:00,840 --> 00:20:12,160
For instance, if an item has a conversion limit of three, and there are three other players who have converted that item into a card already, then that's it.

323
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:16,420
The fourth player who obtains said item cannot change it into a card.

324
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:25,200
In the second case, a card will turn back into an item unless it's in your book within one minute.

325
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:28,760
In this case, it is also irreversible.

326
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:30,920
Do you understand?

327
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:33,560
Yeah. Yeah, kinda.

328
00:20:34,260 --> 00:20:36,940
Finally, the most important word of caution.

329
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:40,580
My brain is getting full.

330
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:46,320
In this game, whenever a player dies, both their binder and their ring are destroyed.

331
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:48,800
And the contents will cease to exist.

332
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:52,240
I don't think that would matter much to a dead person.

333
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:55,040
That concludes my explanation.

334
00:20:55,640 --> 00:21:00,280
You will need to learn about all of the other aspects of the game by playing it for yourself.

335
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,800
Right. I understand. And thanks a lot.

336
00:21:06,440 --> 00:21:09,320
I wish you the very best of luck on your journey.

337
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:11,420
Now please walk down the stairs.

338
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:21,720
Loading all saved data, I have a message for you from Mr. Gene Freaks.

339
00:21:21,940 --> 00:21:22,440
Gene!

340
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:25,300
Glad to see you made it in, Gon.

341
00:21:25,840 --> 00:21:27,820
This is the game I made with my friends.

342
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:29,220
Hope you like it.

343
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:34,780
If you thought there'd be a clue to help you find me, though, well, too bad.

344
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:37,600
I just wanted to show off our game.

345
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:46,780
It doesn't matter what brought you here, because you won't be able to leave until you obtain a specific item.

346
00:21:47,780 --> 00:21:48,860
So go ahead.

347
00:21:49,560 --> 00:21:50,500
Play your heart out.

348
00:21:50,500 --> 00:22:03,800
Gohan has finally stepped foot inside the legendary game, Greed Island.

349
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:06,800
A new adventure is about to begin.

350
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:25,240
Good luck.

